### LGPL-3.0-only transitive dependency

protolab transitively links the `malachite` family of Rust crates
(arbitrary-precision arithmetic) via `nickel-lang` via several panproto
crates (`panproto-lens-dsl`, `panproto-theory-dsl`, `panproto-grammars`,
`panproto-parse`). `malachite` is licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License version 3.0 (LGPL-3.0-only).

Use of the LGPL-3.0-only `malachite` crates within protolab is permitted
under Section 4 of the LGPL-3.0, which allows combining LGPL libraries with
software under other licenses. protolab users who wish to exercise their
LGPL rights — specifically, to substitute a modified version of `malachite`
or `nickel-lang` — can do so by adding a Cargo `[patch.crates-io]` entry
that redirects those crates to a local or forked source. Cargo's default
dependency machinery makes this process straightforward without requiring
any protolab source changes.

The `malachite` source code is available at
https://gitlab.com/mitchmindtree/malachite and from crates.io. Its LGPL-3.0
license text is distributed alongside the crate in the Cargo registry.

